// The melody opens with a whole-rest bar; the lyrics skip it with an EXPLICIT
// empty bar - the leading "| |" pair (a lone leading "|" only anchors the run,
// the bare-barline rule). The verse must line up one bar in - "Twin- kle" on the
// first NOTE bar - with NO stray hyphen/extender line drawn over the rest bar.
title "Lyrics after a rest bar"
tempo 100
time 4/4
key c major
octave absolute

part melody { clef treble }

section A { r1 | c'4 c' g' g' | a' a' g'2 | f'4 f' e' e' | d' d' c'2 | }
lyrics words { | | Twin- kle twin- kle | lit- tle star | How I won- der | what you are | }

form main { A }

score main "rest-lyrics" { staff melody with lyrics words }
